# Exemptions for scripts/cfg-audit. One per line: `path:pattern  # reason`, or `path:*<=N  # reason` for a whole file.
# A stale entry (no hit, or a pattern that matches nothing) fails the audit.

# Test-only cfgs in app files: a Windows-only test or a Windows-only part of a test.
src/app/adblock_app.rs:#[cfg(windows)] // test: the DACL  # the access list of a saved file is a Windows fact (SDDL)
src/app/archive_ui.rs:#[cfg(windows)] // an exclusive share mode  # a Windows open flag in a test
src/app/emu_ui.rs:#[cfg(windows)] // junctions (mklink /J)  # the links-and-devices test makes junctions, device names and file symlinks
src/app/menu_hold_tests.rs:#[cfg(windows)]  # a test file for the real HWND and muda Win32 bar
src/app/page_saver_app.rs:#[cfg(windows)] // test: the Mark of the Web  # an NTFS stream test
src/app/statusbar_content.rs:#[cfg(windows)] // test: ICU through Windows  # ICU answers through Windows in this test

# Owning modules outside src/app/: their Windows code sits behind a cfg until it moves under platform/ (P1).
